    "long_instructions": "Before you build anything, it helps to sketch out your plan first, the same way a programmer storyboards before writing code.\r\n\r\n# Do This:\r\n- Pick a topic you care about. \r\n- Sketch a small card or scene that shows off your topic.\r\n- Label your planned variables and draw an arrow from each label to the part of your sketch it describes:\r\n  - At least 3 `string` labels, for things you'll type in later (like a name, a color, or a mascot)\r\n  - 1 `int` label, for a whole number\r\n  - 1 `bool` label, for a true/false detail\r\n- Save your sketch to your Backpack when you're finished. ",
